; The compiler, in one library. Its sources live in folders by stage:
;   syntax/  source text to AST (locations, tokens, lexer, parser)
;   sema/    the checks that run before anything does (resolve, mut, infer,
;            exhaust)
;   core/    what every pass shares: identities (paths), canonical types,
;            interfaces, and the prelude, with its built-ins' types
;   lower/   Core, the typed language a checked program is lowered to, the
;            lowering, Core Lint, and a module's implementation tier
;   eval/    the interpreter, the values it computes, and what the prelude's
;            built-in functions do when they run
; `unqualified` means the folders only organize files: every module keeps
; its plain name (Parser, not Syntax.Parser).

(include_subdirs unqualified)

(library
 (name ren)
 (libraries unix)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_deriving.show)))
